-- `Error` in the static inference (#1143, docs/c1f-error.md section (d)): Error is a KIND (not a null flag, never stripped by `or`); an operation on a value that may be an Error may be an Error; `x is Error` and `why(x)` read it without; the failure sites type as `T | Error`. Converted from tests/error_infer_1143.rs; what stays Rust there is the per-pack getter table.

test an error constructor is the error kind and the type text reads back
type Error('x') = "Error"
type x with x: Int? | Error = "(Int|Error)?"
type x with x: Error = "Error"
type 1 if c else Error('x') with c: Bool = "Int|Error"

test a cast that may fail is its type or error
type Int(x) with x: Text = "Int|Error"
type Int(x) with x: Int = "Int"
type Int(x) with x: Int? = "Int?"
type Int(x) with x: Text? = "(Int|Error)?"
type Int(x) with x: Any = "(Int|Error)?"

test an operation on a value that may be an error may be an error
type x + 1 with x: Int | Error, l: List(Int) | Error, t: Text | Error, c: Bool | Error = "Int|Error"
type -x with x: Int | Error, l: List(Int) | Error, t: Text | Error, c: Bool | Error = "Int|Error"
type l[0] with x: Int | Error, l: List(Int) | Error, t: Text | Error, c: Bool | Error = "(Int|Error)?"
type len(t) with x: Int | Error, l: List(Int) | Error, t: Text | Error, c: Bool | Error = "Int|Error"
type lower(t) with x: Int | Error, l: List(Int) | Error, t: Text | Error, c: Bool | Error = "Text|Error"
type 1 if c else 2 with x: Int | Error, l: List(Int) | Error, t: Text | Error, c: Bool | Error = "Int|Error"
type x == 1 with x: Int | Error, l: List(Int) | Error, t: Text | Error, c: Bool | Error = "Bool|Error"
type not c with x: Int | Error, l: List(Int) | Error, t: Text | Error, c: Bool | Error = "Bool|Error"
type [y for y in l] with x: Int | Error, l: List(Int) | Error, t: Text | Error, c: Bool | Error = "List(Int)|Error"
findings x + 1 with x: Int | Error, l: List(Int) | Error, t: Text | Error, c: Bool | Error = 0

test is and why and a null test read an error without propagating
type x is Error with x: Int | Error = "Bool"
type x is not Error with x: Int | Error = "Bool"
type x == None with x: Int | Error = "Bool"
type why(x) with x: Int | Error = "Any"

test the class and text of a reason read without a finding
findings why(x).cls with x: Int | Error = 0
findings why(x).text with x: Int | Error = 0
findings why(x) is Refused with x: Int | Error = 0

test or is a default that never hides an error
type x or 0 with x: Int? | Error = "Int|Error"
type x or 0 with x: Int? = "Int"
